A successful demo does not prove that an AI agent is ready for production. Production readiness means a team can state the outcome, control the agent’s authority, observe representative behavior, recover from failure, and name the person who owns the service after launch. This guide is for engineering leaders and delivery teams moving a real workflow beyond its prototype. It does not replace domain-specific risk review, legal approval, or a service-level agreement.

{% trace-scenario title="Is this agent ready to launch?" prompt="The happy path works, but there is no owner for quality regressions after release. What is missing?" outcome="Production readiness includes ownership, observable outcomes, failure handling, evaluation, and rollback—not only a successful demo. If nobody owns the next decision, the launch gate is incomplete." /%}

